## Summary

Adds a standalone, dependency-free Tor agent access client for the canonical VOID public onion service.

The client:

- uses SOCKS5 domain addressing so `.onion` names are resolved by Tor, not local DNS;
- verifies the signed Ed25519 node-to-onion binding against a pinned node-key fingerprint;
- validates Tor v3 address checksums and binding/descriptor aliases;
- pins exact required DataNet public contract bodies;
- reports missing optional discovery surfaces honestly;
- distinguishes an advertised read-only MCP descriptor from proven MCP execution;
- performs no node, Tor, wallet, ledger, payment, or fund mutation.

